{
  "category": "Flower Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "A carnivorous POKéMON that traps and eats bugs. It uses its root feet to soak up needed moisture.",
      "version": "red"
    },
    {
      "text": "A carnivorous POKéMON that traps and eats bugs. It uses its root feet to soak up needed moisture.",
      "version": "blue"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prefers hot and humid places. It ensnares tiny insects with its vines and devours them.",
      "version": "yellow"
    },
    {
      "text": "Even though its body is extremely skinny, it is blindingly fast when catching its prey.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "It plants its feet deep underground to replenish wa ter. It can't escape its enemy while it's rooted.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "If it notices anything that moves, it immediately flings its vine at the object.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "BELLSPROUT’s thin and flexible body lets it bend and sway to avoid any attack, however strong it may be. From its mouth, this POKéMON spits a corrosive fluid that melts even iron.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "BELLSPROUT’s thin and flexible body lets it bend and sway to avoid any attack, however strong it may be. From its mouth, this POKéMON spits a corrosive fluid that melts even iron.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "A BELLSPROUT’s thin and flexible body lets it bend and sway to avoid any attack, however strong it may be. From its mouth, it leaks a fluid that melts even iron.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
